# The web trial's headers — paper 122, rules 85 and 86.
#
# **This file is a record, like `site/_headers`**: the server sends the
# headers, and this is what they should be for the trial's pages, kept beside
# the page so the intent is reviewed with it. `flutter build web` copies it into
# the build, so it stands in `site-trial/` too.
#
# What differs from the site's own policy, and why:
#
# * `script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'` — the page's scripts and the two
#   WebAssembly modules (Flutter's CanvasKit and Z's core, `z_web_bg.wasm`)
#   come from our own origin. `'wasm-unsafe-eval'` compiles WebAssembly and
#   nothing else: no `'unsafe-eval'`, no `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts.
# * `connect-src 'self'` — the page can reach no host but ours, so the
#   visitor's text cannot leave the browser even by a fault of ours.
# * `style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'` — **the trial only, the lead's ruling of
#   13 November 2026.** Flutter's engine injects two `<style>` elements with
#   its text-editing rules (they hide the hidden input's own caret, selection
#   and placeholder). Inline style cannot reach the network while
#   `connect-src`, `img-src` and `font-src` are `'self'`, and per-browser
#   hashes of those two elements would break on the next Flutter or browser
#   update. Measured in headless Chrome: with this policy the page reports no
#   violation at all.
# * No `<base>`, no manifest, no service worker: `base-uri 'none'` and
#   `default-src 'none'` stay as the site has them, and leaving the page keeps
#   nothing (rule 85 (c)).
# * No COOP/COEP: the core and the renderer need no shared memory.
# * `frame-src 'self'` — paper 124: Scribe's editor opens over the trial in an
#   `<iframe>` of our own origin (`/<lang>/try/scribe/`). Nothing else may be
#   framed; nothing may frame the trial (`frame-ancestors 'none'`).
#
# **Scribe's page, `/*/try/scribe/*`**, is the one page that may be framed,
# and only by our own origin: the rule below takes the two headers of `/*`
# that forbid it off (`! Name`, as Cloudflare's `_headers` writes a detach) and
# sends its own — the same policy, with `frame-ancestors 'self'` and
# `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN`, and without `frame-src` (it frames nothing).
# The other three headers of `/*` stay as they are. The server's record,
# `_trial.nginx`, is written from these two rules.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; connect-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; frame-src 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), interest-cohort=()

/*/try/scribe/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  ! X-Frame-Options
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; connect-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
